+# ĐÌNH ĐƯỢC- VOICE STUDIO custom Windows build
+
+The fixed RSA public key in `config/license-authority.json` verifies machine-bound
+activation codes issued by the owner's separate tool. The signing key is never
+included in this app. Invalid, expired and other-machine codes cannot start the
+backend. An expired running session restarts into activation. Windows DPAPI protects
+the saved token and last-seen time. Offline licensing cannot promise tamper-proof
+clock/source-code enforcement or remote revocation.
+
+The custom app uses `DinhDuocVoiceStudio` as its separate user-data directory and
+backend port 43900. It does not install upstream automatic updates. The owner
+can distribute the app ZIP and issued codes to friends; the issuer tool stays
+with the owner. AGPL notices and corresponding source remain available.
+
+## Sentence pauses
+
+TXT line mode inserts 500 ms of silence between non-empty lines by default. The
+script panel offers 0–5000 ms in 100 ms steps. No leading or trailing silence is
+added. A following SRT cue starts after that same silence in the waveform. Existing
+recordings must be regenerated to apply the new pause. Normal whole-paragraph
+synthesis and voice design retain their existing behavior.
+
+## Pause and resume a TXT batch
+
+The clone composer offers Pause and Resume while Audio + SRT line mode is running,
+including multiple imported TXT files. Pause waits for the current sentence to
+finish, then stops at the next sentence boundary. The status distinguishes a
+pending pause from an acknowledged pause. Resume retains in-memory sentence audio
+and continues without re-synthesizing completed sentences or completed TXT files.
+The SRT clock counts audio samples and configured inter-sentence silence only;
+time spent waiting at a manual pause never changes caption timestamps.
+
+Controls are local, in-memory and apply only while the app remains open. Closing
+the app or cancelling discards incomplete-file progress. Already exported files
+remain on disk. The cancel button remains available while paused. A disconnected
+request is cancelled at a sentence boundary; inactive controls are cleaned up.
+Controlled requests keep the backend's per-sentence inference limits, but omit
+the frontend's wall-clock backstop so a deliberate pause does not time out.
